<title>USA: GM Corp unit GMAC may set $500 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>GM Corp unit GMAC may set $500 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp unit, General Motors Acceptance Corp (GMAC), may issue $500 million in a global debt offering, syndicate sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The A3/A-minus rated deal is expected to include a five-year floating rate note. Unofficial price talk on the issue is seen at 18-20 basis points over the three-month libor rate, sources said.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to be underwritten by Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc and UBS Securities, sources added.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
